Subject: rangers, arrows vs. daggers, and 2 steps short of a YASD

It has been a _very_ long time since I've had a game
last this long (over 50,000 turns and counting), and
I can feel the RNG just gnashing its incredibly
sharp and poisonous teeth finding ways to offer me a
YASD [I haven't seen a =oSD yet, so I think I know
what it will be: you doze off at the keyboard, you
hunger, you weaken, you faint, you get stomped, your
very own "while helpless" tombstone shows up on the
screen, where "while stupid" would be more accurate].

But meanwhile, just a comment: by the time I had the
ability to bless, enchant, and fix weapons, I was
down to too few arrows to matter, it wasn't worth
wasting the consumables on arrows any more, so my
ranger is happily flinging sets of daggers from a
stock of 21 +3 rustproof daggers. Is it just my
imagination, or does the usual game contain far too
few arrows, compared to the time when you can
enhance the survival prospects of arrows, even if
you successfully untrap every trap and harvest every
dropped kit from a humanoid, to make it worth
enhancing "bow" skills even for a ranger?

I've been picking up arrows in carload lots since I
gave up using them, and may revert from "expert
daggers" to "expert bow" just to see what the next
level above "expert" is called, since my PC is maxed
out on daggers but still has growing room to enhance
bow when I make Xp 14, but there seems to be a definite
bottleneck point where your ranger better have
developed some other skill than yeoman archer, to
survive.

By the way, the deepest I've been is DLVL 12 in
mines and DLVL 11 on the main branch; the first
altar I could convert was _below_ the entrance to
mines, which is why all the necessaries for
bettering weapons and armor arrived so late in the
game.

Nicest single possession right now is blessed +4
water walking boots, which made it _way_ worthwhile
to convert the fountain at the bottom of mines and
one around DLVL 8 of the main branch to pools, for
ease in #dip-ing. Though my character sneers at the
stuff that comes out of a fountain, any more, pools
don't seem to dry up, a much better deal.

Things are looking _so_ good

    [I'm AC -33 HP 106 Pw 93 Xp 13/43569 (all
    earned, I fed the wraith corpses to the pets).
    I'm wielding +6 fixed Sting, and carrying some
    bones pile +2 SDSM until I can uncurse it, but
    my well enchanted elven mithral is doing fine
    for now. I've IDed most of the potions and many
    of the dangerous scrolls (lack knowing "tower of
    flame" still). My naked AC is 2 and the Mines
    Town cross-aligned priestess is considering a
    condo in the Alps somewhere if she lives to
    retirement age, since a lot of this protection
    was bought at Xp 10 and 11. All the shopkeepers
    are still alive, all but Izchak are broke and
    looking at bare shelves. I'm keeping mostly
    around 5 pets alive at once for company, but
    going through them very fast as they foolishly
    take on monsters twice their size. I've done all
    of Mines, all of Sokoban, cleaned out one small
    throne room and one leprechaun hall. I am still
    wishless, genoless and polyless, but spent a
    while as a kobold lord due to an inconveniently
    placed polytrap before I switched my plussed
    rotted elven cloak for an unplussed robe. I even
    know half a dozen spells I can cast if I take
    the time to strip to my socks first, though they
    are all expired right now and need restudy,
    which was nice when I had an U?oEW for fixing
    the daggers.]

that I'm pretty sure the RNG is calling in fellow
